## Gate (roadmap 2.6)

- F3 as in the first run (no preprocessing), leave-one-strain-out: 0.200 [0.12, 0.26] (F3/knn), chance 0.050 -> CI above chance.
- F3.bg with nearest centroid (pre-specified for 2b), leave-one-strain-out: 0.192 [0.11, 0.26] (F3.bg/ncm), chance 0.050 -> CI above chance.
- F3.ctrl with nearest centroid (pre-specified for 2b; control culture subtracted), leave-one-strain-out: 0.082 [0.02, 0.15] (F3.ctrl/ncm), chance 0.050 -> **CI includes chance.**
- best F3 family, leave-one-strain-out: 0.217 [0.13, 0.29], p=0.001 (F3.snv/plsda), chance 0.050 -> CI above chance.
- LR on F1 (string, pre-specified), leave-one-strain-out: 0.120 [0.05, 0.19], p=0.032 (F1/lr), chance 0.050 -> CI above chance.
- LR on F1.bg (pre-specified for 2b), leave-one-strain-out: 0.103 [0.04, 0.16] (F1.bg/lr), chance 0.050 -> **CI includes chance.**
- best F1 family, leave-one-strain-out: 0.120 [0.05, 0.19], p=0.032 (F1/lr), chance 0.050 -> CI above chance.
- per culture (majority vote over a culture's scans, n = 40): 0.225 [0.12, 0.32] (F3.snv/plsda)
- best F3 family - best F1 family = +0.097: how much the string format loses.

## Detectability (no classifier involved)

An analyte's signature = its culture mean minus the strain mean. r_cross = correlation of the signature between the two strains; rank = where the matching analyte ranks in the other strain (1 = best match); r_std = correlation with the pure standard; snr = signature size / scan noise.

