# T2 baselines (native)

Primary metric: AUROC. Values: point [95% bootstrap CI over cultures / analytes / molecules], p = group-permutation p-value.
"Best" columns pick the best non-majority model over a feature family (F3 = F3, F3.bg, F3.d1 ...). They are chosen on the test result, so read them as optimistic; LR on F1 is the pre-specified number.
lpo:* rows are leave-pair-out AUROC at analyte level: one positive and one negative analyte are held out together and only their two scores, from the same model, are compared. This replaces the pooled leave-one-analyte-out AUROC of the first run, which was biased downward.

